This is a port of mgif for the ST to OS9it runs on ST's only, if you don't change the source.There is a display routine in flicker.c called _Conv2Gray, which writesto the grafikmemory which has to be changed.The printer image routine, which creates file "ausgabe.img" for printout, hasto be changed too (just cancel the writes to grafikmemory or replace themwith the proper code for your grafik device).The rest is plain OSK. Grafikroutines are contained in gpprim.r.The file primg.c contains a program to create a printerfile for aHP Printer from a .img (GEM-image) file. It works on my DeskJet anshould work with a LaserJet. The Program takes the filename and optionalresolution and quality as input and creates a printerfile in file "xx".To print just do:copy xx /p                if "/p" is your printer device.To use the program, you need 1.4 MB of available memory in one block.tmode nopausemgif -N <giffile>"type space and wait. when the picture appears hit any key to make itflicker faster.""type '?' to get the menu (several times)"/* the option 'x' does not appear on the screen, but is there. */"type 'x' to create 'ausgabe.img' ""choose 'g' for best quality. wait. If the cursor is back type 'q'"primg ausgabe.img       "and wait"copy xx /p              "enjoy ???"I have included some gif pictures for you to test the stuff.make with make ./mgif